      ],
      "text": "Detection of pulmonary TB",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Md",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        96.54881286621094,
        512.7697143554688,
        110.63681030273438
      ],
      "text": "Should LC-aNAATs on respiratory samples be used to diagnose pulmonary TB in",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-MdIt",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        110.94883728027344,
        504.01580810546875,
        125.03683471679688
      ],
      "text": "adults and adolescents with signs and symptoms or who screened positive for",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-MdIt",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        125.34880065917969,
        406.8686218261719,
        139.43679809570312
      ],
      "text": "pulmonary TB, against a microbiological reference standard?",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-MdIt",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        150.10382080078125,
        526.9591064453125,
        163.2488250732422
      ],
      "text": "Thirty-five studies (14 845 participants) assessed diagnostic accuracy using sputum specimens",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        165.60382080078125,
        526.7335205078125,
        178.7488250732422
      ],
      "text": "and comparing with a microbiological reference standard (MRS); however, one of those studies",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 10.962435722351074,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.10382080078125,
        527.0360717773438,
        194.2488250732422
      ],
      "text": "had no people with TB (Zar 2019) and so sensitivity was not estimable. The sensitivities in",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        196.60382080078125,
        526.9588623046875,
        209.7488250732422
      ],
      "text": "the remaining 34 studies (14 840 participants) included in the meta-analysis were between",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        212.10382080078125,
        526.9639282226562,
        225.2488250732422
      ],
      "text": "54% and 100%, and the specificities were between 71% and 100% ( ). The summary  Fig. 2.1.1",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        227.60382080078125,
        526.9645385742188,
        240.7488250732422
      ],
      "text": "sensitivity was 90.4% (95% confidence interval [CI]: 88.0–92.4), and the summary specificity",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        243.10382080078125,
        526.9185791015625,
        256.24884033203125
      ],
      "text": "was 94.9% (95% CI: 93.0–96.3). The certainty of evidence for sensitivity and specificity was",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        258.60382080078125,
        344.91650390625,
        271.74884033203125
      ],
      "text": "graded as “high”. For more details, see  . Web Annex B.1",
      "font": "FrutigerNeueLT-Lt",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        286.3900146484375,
        506.11810302734375,
        300.4779968261719
      ],
